    // which is address-derived and differs between two runs of the SAME program, so
    // nothing can assert the digits; what matters is that one object renders the
    // same way twice and that the run is reproducible. So: the k-th distinct object
    // rendered gets 0x1a2b3c00+k, in hex - and abnf/jsrtjava.go's jvpHash does the
    // identical thing, so the two halves agree object for object.
